    "title": "Former Ramada Inn in Augusta converted to apartments - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rakiyah Lenon ,\n5 hours ago\nAUGUSTA, Ga. (WJBF) – There’s new life for a former hotel in Augusta.\nWhat used to be a Ramada Inn on Reservation Way off Gordon Highway is now a multi-family apartment complex. It’s located a mile away from Fort Gordon and can serve as additional housing for the military.\nA ribbon cutting was held on Wednesday, Feb. 25 to mark the opening.\n“We have 150 units and it’s called smart living. Our units are about 300 square feet and we offer a lot of amenities,” said Jaylah Jackson, community manager of the 210 Club. “So it’s great for military, traveling nurses, anybody that likes to live simple.”\nThe apartment complex has a pool, gym, business center, dog park, fire pit areas, gaming and lounge areas.\nPhotojournalist credit: Regynal McKie\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJBF.\n5",
    "summary": "What used to be a Ramada Inn on Reservation Way off Gordon Highway is now a multi-family apartment complex. It’s located a mile away from Fort Gordon and can serve as additional housing for the military. Our units are about 300 square feet and we offer a lot of amenities,” said Jaylah Jackson, community manager of the 210 Club. “So it’s great for military, traveling nurses, anybody that likes to live simple.” The apartment complex has a pool, gym, business center, dog park, fire pit areas, gaming and lounge areas.",
